# /etc/ebooktrivia/restic.env (0640 root:<app user>): the secondary backup (US-015, infra/backup/restic-backup.sh): every night the
# pg_dump -Fc of ebooktrivia, the pg_dumpall --globals-only and /srv/data go into a restic repository (encrypted with RESTIC_PASSWORD) on
# S3-compatible storage; 7 daily, 4 weekly and 6 monthly snapshots are kept. Use ANOTHER bucket than wal-g\x27s, ideally another provider,
# so one account or one bucket policy cannot lose both copies. host-check.sh fails while __SET_ME__ is left.
#   RESTIC_REPOSITORY  s3:https://<endpoint>/<bucket>/restic
# RESTIC_PASSWORD is generated by provision.sh, once: escrow it the day it is made (docs/escrow.md); without it the repository is lost.
# The file is passed to the one-shot restic container with --env-file; it is in no image and no unit file.
RESTIC_REPOSITORY=__SET_ME__
RESTIC_PASSWORD=@GEN@
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=__SET_ME__
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=__SET_ME__
AWS_DEFAULT_REGION=__SET_ME__
